        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-71002",
        ":question/problem": "If $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x-11\\pi ).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-11$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-11)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-11\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ we get that $tan⁡(x-11\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$"
